# CITATION.cff — awkronos/web (Agent Data Pod Specification)
#
# Every value below is measured from origin/main@88870343c6ec3f0d4d4e90b01fefab93c59274e3
# or from `gh api repos/awkronos/web` (2026-11-03). Fields that could not be measured are
# OMITTED, never invented: no DOI, ORCID, arXiv id or funder appears in this file, because
# none appears in this repository's own text. RFC 2119, PROV-O and RDF Dataset
# Canonicalization were additionally checked on their canonical pages and carry no DOI
# there either — for the standards this profile is built on, the stable identifier is the
# versioned URL, which is what `references:` records.
#
# `license` = CC-BY-4.0, measured from three independent places in this repo:
#   package.json ("license": "CC-BY-4.0"), vocab.ttl (dct:license
#   <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>), and the site footer
#   ("An Awkronos for humans project · CC BY 4.0 · 2026 Timothy Jacoby").
#   GitHub's detector reports no license because no LICENSE file is tracked — a repo gap,
#   not a different license. NOT guessed.
#
# `version` / `date-released` / `commit` = 0.2.0, dated 2026-02-03 by changelog.html
#   (0.1.0 = 2026-02-01); `commit` is the full SHA of main at the time this file was written.
#
# `authors` = person + org. Measured basis: package.json `author` and vocab.ttl
#   `dct:creator` (foaf:name "Timothy Jacoby", foaf:mbox tim@awkronos.com); site footer
#   "2026 Timothy Jacoby"; git history = 18 commits, 16 by Chronos Bot identities that carry
#   no personal name, 2 by Tim Jacoby. The project's citation law forbids a bare org as sole
#   author where persons authored. ORCID is omitted rather than guessed.
#
# ROOT `type` is OMITTED deliberately: the 1.2.0 enum is [dataset | software] only, and a
#   specification profile is neither. Omitting is more truthful than asserting `software`
#   for a normative document set. This is the same 1.2.0 expressiveness gap that makes
#   contributorship inexpressible (no root `contributors`, no root `year` — verified against
#   schema.json at ref 1.2.0: root required = [authors, cff-version, message, title],
#   21 allowed root keys, additionalProperties false). Per-unit `kind` and full
#   contributorship therefore live in docs/CITATIONS.md, which is the load-bearing leg.
#
# `references:` = the 11 external works this repository itself names in a References section
#   (spec.html §6 normative [5] + informative [3], paper.html §7 adds DID-CORE,
#   interop.html adds ANP Agent Description) plus RFC 9449, which spec.html §5.7 cites
#   normatively in prose while omitting it from §6. Publisher-as-entity names are copied from
#   this repository's own reference labels, not assigned. FOAF, DC Terms (namespace imports in
#   vocab.ttl) and OpenMemory HMD v2 (named, never linked) are recorded in docs/CITATIONS.md.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this project, please cite it as below. Per-result, structured citations
  (each citable unit with its kind, authors, epistemic status, stable link and citation
  graph) are in docs/CITATIONS.md — that file, not this one, is the authoritative citation
  carrier, because CFF 1.2.0 cannot express contributorship.
title: >-
  Agent Data Pod Specification: A profile of the Solid Protocol for AI agent data storage
  (draft, v0.2.0)
authors:
  - given-names: Timothy
    family-names: Jacoby
    email: tim@awkronos.com
  - name: Awkronos
repository-code: https://github.com/awkronos/web
url: https://awkronos.github.io/web/
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-02-03"
commit: 88870343c6ec3f0d4d4e90b01fefab93c59274e3
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A draft profile of the Solid Protocol for storing AI agent data — memory episodes, agent
  state, capability declarations and audit trails — in user-controlled Solid Pods, so that
  an agent's accumulated context can migrate between implementations. The normative content
  is spec.html (14 requirement clauses [A1]-[A6] and [S1]-[S8], carrying 32 RFC 2119 keywords)
  and vocab.ttl (25 terms: 6 OWL classes and 19 properties, 17 datatype / 2 object, with
  agent:AIAgent subclassed under foaf:Agent and agent:MemoryEpisode / agent:AuditEntry under
  prov:Entity / prov:Activity). Conformance is levelled Minimal / Standard / Full. This
  repository contains no proofs, no conformance suite and no experiments: every claim is
  design intent, and the specification states it "has not been reviewed or endorsed by any
  standards body."
keywords:
  - solid
  - agent
  - ai
  - rdf
  - specification
  - data-sovereignty
  - memory
  - interoperability
references:
  - abbreviation: RFC-2119
    authors:
      - name: Internet Engineering Task Force
    title: Key words for use in RFCs to Indicate Requirement Levels
    type: standard
    url: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc2119
    year: 1997
    notes: spec.html §1.1; normative in spec.html §6
  - abbreviation: RFC-9449
    authors:
      - name: Internet Engineering Task Force
    title: >-
      OAuth 2.0 Demonstrating Proof of Possession (DPoP)
    type: standard
    url: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9449
    year: 2023
    notes: >-
      spec.html §5.7 [S7] cites "RFC 9449" in prose; DPoP named there, title verified on the
      IETF page. Absent from spec.html §6 References — a dangling normative reference.
  - abbreviation: SOLID-PROTOCOL
    authors:
      - name: Solid Project
    title: "Solid Protocol, Version 0.11.0"
    type: standard
    url: https://solidproject.org/TR/protocol
    year: 2024
    notes: >-
      Normative base of this profile. "Version 0.11.0, May 2024" measured from paper.html §7.
  - abbreviation: WAC
    authors:
      - name: Solid Project
    title: Web Access Control
    type: standard
    url: https://solid.github.io/web-access-control-spec/
    notes: spec.html §6 normative; used by requirement [S3]
  - abbreviation: PROV-O
    authors:
      - name: World Wide Web Consortium
    title: "PROV-O: The PROV Ontology"
    type: standard
    url: https://www.w3.org/TR/2013/REC-prov-o-20130430/
    year: 2013
    notes: >-
      Dated W3C Recommendation permalink (30 April 2013), verified against the W3C page;
      persistent latest-version URL is https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/. Superclasses
      prov:Entity and prov:Activity in vocab.ttl. No DOI on the canonical page.
  - abbreviation: RDFC-1.0
    authors:
      - name: World Wide Web Consortium
    title: RDF Dataset Canonicalization
    type: standard
    url: https://w3c.github.io/rdf-canon/spec/
    notes: >-
      spec.html §6 normative; used by requirement [S5] integrity hashing and agent:contentHash.
      Status/version of this document not asserted here — no dated version was verified.
  - abbreviation: DID-CORE
    authors:
      - name: World Wide Web Consortium
    title: "Decentralized Identifiers (DIDs) v1.0"
    type: standard
    url: https://www.w3.org/TR/did-core/
    year: 2022
    notes: paper.html §7 — "W3C Recommendation, July 2022"
  - abbreviation: DID-WBA
    authors:
      - name: Agent Network Protocol
    title: ANP did:wba Method Specification
    type: standard
    url: https://agentnetworkprotocol.com/en/specs/03-did-wba-method-specification/
    notes: spec.html §6 informative; interop.html; identity linkage in [S6]
  - abbreviation: ANP-AGENT-DESCRIPTION
    authors:
      - name: Agent Network Protocol
    title: ANP Agent Description Protocol Specification
    type: standard
    url: https://agentnetworkprotocol.com/en/specs/07-anp-agent-description-protocol-specification/
    notes: interop.html; defines agent:AgentDescriptionService (rdfs:seeAlso)
  - abbreviation: A2A
    authors:
      - name: A2A Protocol
    title: Agent2Agent Protocol Specification
    type: standard
    url: https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/specification/
    notes: >-
      spec.html §6 informative; interop.html. Cited as "/latest/" — no fixed version of record.
  - abbreviation: MCP
    authors:
      - name: Model Context Protocol
    title: Model Context Protocol Specification
    type: standard
    url: https://modelcontextprotocol.io/
    notes: >-
      spec.html §6 informative; paper.html §7; interop.html; agent:mcpEndpoint.
      interop.html also links /specification/2025-11-25 as a dated snapshot.
